WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.839
Your next offer is hiding in public complaints.

00:00:02.839 --> 00:00:04.614
Listen where people already vent.

00:00:04.614 --> 00:00:07.453
This lesson is about problem hunting in public.

00:00:07.453 --> 00:00:08.872
Listen where people complain.

00:00:08.872 --> 00:00:11.357
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:11.357 --> 00:00:14.906
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.906 --> 00:00:20.229
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.229 --> 00:00:24.133
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:28.392
Stay practical: capture three buyer phrases before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.712 --> 00:00:34.449
Hunt in forums, comment threads, review sites, and group chats where your buyers hang out.

00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:37.127
Remember the objective: capture three buyer phrases.

00:00:37.127 --> 00:00:41.334
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:45.924
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.924 --> 00:00:50.131
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:50.131 --> 00:00:54.721
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.398
Talk to a real person when possible.

